    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-149da17b",
      "dossier_scope": "hardware",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "hardware"
        ],
        "entry_type": "recipe",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "procedural",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "**Hardware-portable**: all hardware-specific configuration (pin map, bike signal set, partition table, SDK settings) lives in one target directory under `hardware/`. A different ESP32 board or bike is a new target directory plus a PlatformIO environment. Firmware uses `#if HAS_*` guards for bike signals and `WITH_*` flags for compiled modules (§12.3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-4ffa8947",
      "dossier_scope": "framework/hardware/esp32s3nano",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "framework/hardware/_common/board_contract.h",
          "framework/hardware/_TEMPLATE",
          "framework/hardware/esp32s3nano/board.h"
        ],
        "entry_type": "contract",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "semantic",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "**One header.** `board.h` is the single source of truth for pins and bike signals. It follows the framework's board contract (`framework/hardware/_common/board_contract.h`) and is authored from the framework's `framework/hardware/_TEMPLATE/`, not cloned from the reference `framework/hardware/esp32s3nano/board.h`, whose display and button pins collide with Echenon's tap pins (§12.3). No other p..."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-2dda879b",
      "dossier_scope": "root",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "platformio.ini"
        ],
        "entry_type": "invariant",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "semantic",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "**Two flag families.** `HAS_*` macros in `board.h` state that a bike signal exists and is wired. `WITH_*` build flags in `platformio.ini` select which framework and application modules compile (§12.3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-1914be52",
      "dossier_scope": "root",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "sdkconfig.defaults"
        ],
        "entry_type": "recipe",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "procedural",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "**Build wiring.** The PlatformIO env passes `-DBOARD_HEADER=\\\"hardware/ex3-waveshare-nano/board.h\\\"`, the target's partition table and the target's `sdkconfig.defaults` (§12.2)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-678b3000",
      "dossier_scope": "docs",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "docs/ex3_specification.md"
        ],
        "entry_type": "invariant",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "semantic",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "The cadence, potentiometer and encoder signals operate at 3.3 V logic (see [`docs/ex3_specification.md` §10](docs/ex3_specification.md#10-voltage-summary)). They reach the ESP32 only through series resistors (§4.4)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "docseed-fa409e1c",
      "dossier_scope": "root",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T21:07:26Z",
      "source": "doc-seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "sdkconfig.defaults"
        ],
        "entry_type": "invariant",
        "evidence": [
          "doc:SPEC.md"
        ],
        "kind": "semantic",
        "source_doc_blob_sha": "91a27d41f2d70402d69a413f599136d147ad5cb0",
        "source_doc_path": "SPEC.md",
        "text": "**SDK config chain.** The project-root `sdkconfig.defaults` holds the project-level defaults. The framework's `sync_sdkconfig.py` pre-script keeps it in step with the framework root file, as it does for the template app. The framework BLE defaults follow, and the target's own `sdkconfig.defaults` comes last, so the target's octal-PSRAM, 16 MB flash, USB-console and NimBLE slot settings win."
      }
    },
